{"html":"<p>Rust ships as a set of tools, not a single compiler. Understanding what each\npiece does saves you hours later.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-pieces\">The pieces</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Tool</th>\n<th>What it is</th>\n<th>You use it for</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>rustup</code></td>\n<td>Toolchain installer and version manager</td>\n<td>Installing Rust, switching versions, adding targets</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>rustc</code></td>\n<td>The compiler</td>\n<td>Almost never called directly</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>cargo</code></td>\n<td>Build system + package manager + test runner</td>\n<td>Everything</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>rustfmt</code></td>\n<td>Auto-formatter</td>\n<td><code>cargo fmt</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>clippy</code></td>\n<td>Linter with ~750 checks</td>\n<td><code>cargo clippy</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>rust-analyzer</code></td>\n<td>Language server</td>\n<td>Editor autocomplete, inline errors</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>rustdoc</code></td>\n<td>Documentation generator</td>\n<td><code>cargo doc --open</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>You install <code>rustup</code>. <code>rustup</code> installs the rest.</p>\n<h2 id=\"install\">Install</h2>\n<p><strong>Linux / macOS:</strong></p>\n<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=\"\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\"><code data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"display: grid;\"><span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">$</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> curl</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> --proto</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> '=https'</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> --tlsv1.2</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> -sSf</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> https://sh.rustup.rs</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\"> |</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> sh</span></span></code></pre></figure>\n<p><strong>Windows:</strong> download and run <a href=\"https://rustup.rs\">rustup-init.exe</a>. You will be\nasked to install the <strong>Visual Studio C++ Build Tools</strong> — accept it. Rust uses\nthe system linker, and on Windows that means MSVC. (The <code>x86_64-pc-windows-gnu</code>\ntarget avoids this but causes more problems than it solves.)</p>\n<p><strong>Then, in a fresh shell:</strong></p>\n<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=\"\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\"><code data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"display: grid;\"><span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">$</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> rustc</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> --version</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">rustc</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> 1.85.0</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> (4d91de4e4 </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">2025-02-17</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">)</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"> </span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">$</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> cargo</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> --version</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">cargo</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> 1.85.0</span></span></code></pre></figure>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Gotcha:</strong> if <code>cargo: command not found</code>, your shell has not re-read its\nprofile. Run <code>source \"$HOME/.cargo/env\"</code> or open a new terminal. On Windows\nthis is almost always a PATH issue fixed by restarting the terminal.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2 id=\"what-rustup-actually-manages\">What rustup actually manages</h2>\n<p><code>rustup</code> keeps <em>toolchains</em> side by side and switches between them per project.</p>\n<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=\"\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\"><code data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"display: grid;\"><span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">$</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> rustup</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> show</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\">                    # active toolchain, installed targets</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">$</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> rustup</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> update</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\">                  # update everything to latest stable</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">$</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> rustup</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> toolchain</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> list</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\">          # stable, beta, nightly, plus pinned versions</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">$</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> rustup</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> toolchain</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> install</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> 1.75.0</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">$</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> rustup</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> default</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> stable</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">$</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> rustup</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> component</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> add</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> clippy</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> rustfmt</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">$</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> rustup</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> target</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> add</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> wasm32-unknown-unknown</span></span></code></pre></figure>\n<h3 id=\"channels\">Channels</h3>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Channel</th>\n<th>Meaning</th>\n<th>Use for</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>stable</code></td>\n<td>Released every 6 weeks, guaranteed backwards compatible</td>\n<td>Everything production</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>beta</code></td>\n<td>Next stable, for testing</td>\n<td>Catching breakage early</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>nightly</code></td>\n<td>Daily, enables unstable features via <code>#![feature(...)]</code></td>\n<td>Experiments, some tooling</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Rule: use stable.</strong> Nightly is a research tool, not a default. The one common\nexception is <code>cargo +nightly fmt</code> for unstable formatting options, and\n<code>cargo miri</code> for undefined-behaviour checking.</p>\n<h3 id=\"pin-the-toolchain-per-project\">Pin the toolchain per project</h3>\n<p>Create <code>rust-toolchain.toml</code> in the repo root:</p>\n<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=\"\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"toml\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\"><code data-language=\"toml\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"display: grid;\"><span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">[</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">toolchain</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">]</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">channel = </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\"1.85.0\"</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">components = [</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\"rustfmt\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\"clippy\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">]</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">targets = [</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\"x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">]</span></span></code></pre></figure>\n<p>Now anyone who runs <code>cargo build</code> in that directory gets exactly 1.85.0 —\nrustup downloads it automatically. This is the single highest-value file in a\nRust repo for reproducibility, and it costs six lines.</p>\n<h2 id=\"editions\">Editions</h2>\n<p>Editions let the language change syntax without breaking old code. A crate\ndeclares its edition in <code>Cargo.toml</code>; editions interoperate freely.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Edition</th>\n<th>Landed</th>\n<th>Headline change</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>2015</td>\n<td>1.0</td>\n<td>Original</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2018</td>\n<td>1.31</td>\n<td><code>use</code> paths, <code>dyn Trait</code>, NLL borrow checker</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2021</td>\n<td>1.56</td>\n<td>Disjoint closure captures, <code>IntoIterator</code> for arrays, panic macros</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2024</td>\n<td>1.85</td>\n<td><code>gen</code> keyword, <code>unsafe extern</code>, RPIT lifetime capture, <code>if let</code> temporary scope</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>New projects: use <code>edition = \"2024\"</code> if your toolchain is 1.85+, otherwise\n<code>\"2021\"</code>. There is no performance difference.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Rule of thumb:</strong> an edition is a <em>syntax</em> boundary, not an API boundary.\nCrates on different editions link together with no friction. Do not delay an\nupgrade for \"compatibility\" reasons.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2 id=\"editor-setup\">Editor setup</h2>\n<p><strong>VS Code</strong> — install the <code>rust-analyzer</code> extension. Disable any other Rust\nextension you have; two language servers fight each other.</p>\n<p>Settings worth adding (<code>.vscode/settings.json</code>):</p>\n<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=\"\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"json\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\"><code data-language=\"json\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"display: grid;\"><span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">{</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#8DDB8C\">  \"rust-analyzer.check.command\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\"clippy\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">,</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#8DDB8C\">  \"rust-analyzer.cargo.features\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\"all\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">,</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#8DDB8C\">  \"editor.formatOnSave\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">true</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">,</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#8DDB8C\">  \"[rust]\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">: { </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#8DDB8C\">\"editor.defaultFormatter\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\"rust-lang.rust-analyzer\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> }</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">}</span></span></code></pre></figure>\n<p><code>check.command: clippy</code> makes inline diagnostics come from Clippy instead of\nplain <code>cargo check</code> — you see lint warnings as you type, which is a large\nquality-of-life win.</p>\n<p><strong>Neovim / Emacs / Zed / JetBrains</strong> all speak LSP; point them at\n<code>rust-analyzer</code>. JetBrains has a dedicated Rust plugin (RustRover) with a\ndebugger.</p>\n<p><strong>Debugging:</strong> <code>lldb</code> or <code>gdb</code> work with Rust. For a nicer experience install\n<code>rust-gdb</code> / <code>rust-lldb</code> (ships with rustup) which loads Rust pretty-printers so\nyou can inspect <code>String</code>, <code>Vec</code>, <code>HashMap</code> as values instead of raw pointers.</p>\n<h2 id=\"cargos-global-directories\">Cargo's global directories</h2>\n<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=\"\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\"><code data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"display: grid;\"><span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">~</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">/.cargo/bin/          </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\"># cargo, rustc, rustup, cargo-clippy, installed binaries</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">~</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">/.cargo/registry/     </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\"># downloaded crate sources and index cache</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">~</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">/.cargo/git/          </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\"># git dependencies</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">~</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">/.rustup/toolchains/  </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\"># the actual compilers</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">target/</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\">                # per-project build artifacts (safe to delete)</span></span></code></pre></figure>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Gotcha:</strong> <code>target/</code> grows fast — 2–10 GB for a large workspace is normal.\n<code>cargo clean</code> reclaims it, but you lose all incremental state and the next\nbuild is a full rebuild. For space pressure use <code>cargo-sweep</code> to delete only\nartifacts older than N days.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2 id=\"working-offline\">Working offline</h2>\n<p>Cargo caches everything it downloads. To build without network:</p>\n<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=\"\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\"><code data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"display: grid;\"><span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">$</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> cargo</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> fetch</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\">          # populate the cache for the current project</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">$</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> cargo</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> build</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> --offline</span></span></code></pre></figure>\n<p>For fully air-gapped builds, <code>cargo vendor</code> copies all dependency sources into\n<code>vendor/</code> and a <code>.cargo/config.toml</code> points at them:</p>\n<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=\"\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\"><code data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"display: grid;\"><span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">$</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> cargo</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> vendor</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> vendor/</span></span></code></pre></figure>\n<h2 id=\"verifying-a-healthy-install\">Verifying a healthy install</h2>\n<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=\"\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\"><code data-language=\"bash\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"display: grid;\"><span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">$</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> rustc</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> --version</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> &#x26;&#x26; </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">cargo</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> --version</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">$</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> cargo</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> new</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> /tmp/smoke</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> &#x26;&#x26; </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">cd</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> /tmp/smoke</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">$</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> cargo</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> run</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">Hello,</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> world!</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">$</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> cargo</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> clippy</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> --</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> -D</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> warnings</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">$</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> cargo</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> fmt</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> --check</span></span></code></pre></figure>\n<p>If all five succeed, you have a working Rust development environment.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"exercises\">Exercises</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Install Rust, then install the <code>1.75.0</code> toolchain alongside stable. Print\nboth versions with <code>rustup run 1.75.0 rustc --version</code>.</li>\n<li>Add the <code>wasm32-unknown-unknown</code> target. Confirm it appears in <code>rustup show</code>.</li>\n<li>Create <code>rust-toolchain.toml</code> in a test project pinning <code>1.85.0</code>, then run\n<code>cargo build</code> and watch rustup download it.</li>\n<li>Run <code>cargo new --help</code> and read the full flag list. What does\n<code>--vcs none</code> do, and when would you want it?</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Next:</strong> <a href=\"02-hello-cargo.md\">Hello, Cargo</a></p>"}